    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 items-start justify-between mb-8">
      <div><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">IO Zoom VPS Review</h1><div class="flex gap-4 text-sm text-gray-400"><span>Datacenters: <strong class="text-orange-500">8 US/EU</strong></span><span>Rating: <strong>3.8/5</strong></span></div></div>
      <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="bg-green-600 hover:bg-green-500 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-medium transition">Get a budget VPS →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded-xl p-6 mb-8"><div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4"><span class="text-2xl font-bold">3.8/5</span><span class="text-gray-500">Budget KVM + 10 Gbps DDoS rating</span></div><p class="text-gray-300">IO Zoom is a budget KVM VPS provider with a genuinely global 8-datacenter footprint (US East/West + Frankfurt), true KVM virtualization with full root access on every plan, and 10 Gbps DDoS protection included as standard. Open-source Linux distributions only (CentOS, Fedora, Ubuntu, Debian).</p><p class="text-gray-400 mt-2">Entry plan: $10/mo unmanaged KVM 2GB · managed from $20/mo</p></div>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-8"><div><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-green-400">Pros</h2><ul class="space-y-2"><li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ True KVM virtualization with full root access on all plans</li><li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ 8 data centers across US East/West and Europe (Frankfurt) for latency targeting</li><li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ 10 Gbps DDoS protection included standard — rare at the budget tier</li><li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ Unmetered bandwidth with fair-use limits (2–12 TB by tier)</li><li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ Four open-source Linux distributions (CentOS, Fedora, Ubuntu, Debian)</li><li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ Free migrations from other providers</li><li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ Unmanaged entry at $10/mo / managed with cPanel from $20/mo</li></ul></div><div><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-red-400">Cons</h2><ul class="space-y-2"><li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">⚠️ No explicit uptime SLA published</li><li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">⚠️ cPanel-only management (add-on $35.99/mo) — no Plesk option</li><li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">⚠️ Entry price rose from historical ~$3–4/mo to $10/mo</li><li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">⚠️ No Windows VPS tier advertised on the Linux VPS page</li><li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">⚠️ 8 DCs is far fewer than Vultr's 32+ or DigitalOcean's regional cloud</li></ul></div></div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Key plan snapshot</h2><div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table class="w-full text-sm text-left"><thead><tr class="border-b border-gray-700"><th class="py-3">Plan</th><th>vCPU</th><th>RAM</th><th>SSD</th><th>Bandwidth</th><th>Unmanaged</th><th>Managed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><td class="py-3">KVM 2GB</td><td>2</td><td>2GB</td><td>20GB</td><td>2TB</td><td>$10/mo</td><td>$20/mo</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><td class="py-3">KVM 4GB</td><td>4</td><td>4GB</td><td>40GB</td><td>4TB</td><td>$18/mo</td><td>$35/mo</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><td class="py-3">KVM 8GB</td><td>4</td><td>8GB</td><td>80GB</td><td>6TB</td><td>$35/mo</td><td>$55/mo</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3">KVM 12GB</td><td>6</td><td>12GB</td><td>120GB</td><td>7TB</td><td>$50/mo</td><td>$70/mo</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Who should choose IO Zoom?</h2><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">IO Zoom fits budget developers who want <strong>full root access and true KVM virtualization without artificial restrictions</strong>, latency-sensitive workloads that need a US/EU footprint (including Frankfurt), and Linux-first users who prefer open-source distributions. The 10 Gbps DDoS protection standard and 8-datacenter spread are genuine differentiators at the $10/mo entry.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8">It is not the right fit if you need an explicit uptime SLA, managed Windows VPS, or Plesk instead of cPanel. At $10/mo it also sits well above the ~$3–4/mo historical positioning and RackNerd's $1.99 budget entry — IO Zoom competes on value-per-feature (root + DDoS + 8 DCs), not on absolute lowest price.</p>
